The '''Bayan national football team''' represents [[Bayan]] in international football. TALOD coverage describes Bayan as a direct, physical side, and the team entered the [[2026 AFA World Cup]] in Group E alongside [[Okaiken]] and [[Sanyan]]. The squad announcement noted three players based in Okaiken's J-League: midfielder Dario Voss of Seto Osaki, winger Kofi Mensah of Okami FC, and defender Luka Petrov of Aizawa Tigers.

== Playing style ==

Bayan are generally described as a disciplined, physical team that relies on direct transitions, strong duels, and a high-tempo game out of possession. Their style was highlighted in pre-tournament coverage as the sort of approach that can trouble more technical opponents if they are not fully switched on.

